{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And for a man</b> Three times in the Masorah: ולאיש — ולאיש שתים מכסות / ולאיש בושת בן שאול / ולאיש אשר ישכב — for they are two words: ולאיש. One who lies with a man has cause to be ashamed, as written: ולאיש בושת (and for a man — shame). How so? As we find in R. Eliezer: he would uncover a handbreadth and cover a handbreadth, making it appear as though a demon had seized him — and this is ולאיש שתים מכסות (and for a man — two coverings)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:30.483603960Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}